invariant: INV-43
file: p256_wide_verify.c
catches: p256_verify_equiv_test
reason: the host verifier compares R's X with s where the equation names r,
  so it refuses every signature a signer wrote and accepts a pair whose
  s is that X. bin/p256_verify_equiv_test requires the 32-bit verifier's
  verdict on every signature it tries.

--- old
    return ct_memeq(v_be, r_be, P256_SCALAR_LEN) != 0;
--- new
    return ct_memeq(v_be, s_be, P256_SCALAR_LEN) != 0;
